  "scope": {
    "fidelity": "Original documented camera program using the QEMU DVP source, S3 LCD_CAM and GDMA, and the guest LCD. The generated deterministic pattern exercises data transfer and display. Physical sensor timing, incoming optics, and real-device frame rate were not tested.",
    "c_nominal_source_timing": "30 synthetic source frames/s is a model pacing target for record arrival. The frame counts in this report are completed DMA capture attempts in their individual browser windows.",
    "observation": "The configured dwell begins after guest source transfer. Measured guest start to requested interrupt also includes browser case bookkeeping. Each row is a separate fresh browser guest.",
    "metric_definition": "An attempt begins at armed CAM_START with ten programmed record groups of 15360 bytes. A full-group attempt emits ten source EOFs. A nominal complete VSYNC is the modeled frame-end path after all groups. A true incomplete attempt emits fewer than ten groups. Recovery VSYNC may follow a guest STOP and is counted separately from the nominal path.",
    "ack_limit": "Guest acknowledgments are observed as channel 1 IN success-EOF clear writes between record groups. The first baseline run filtered out MMIO, so its ack and STOP counts are unknown.",
    "warning_limit": "Short and overflow counts are guest diagnostics observed within these windows. A silent recovery can occur without a warning or visual framebuffer difference.",
    "source_archive_scope": "The diagnostic static sites retain the original locked 0042 archive as a baseline control. The candidate-specific C source hashes are listed separately."
  },
